Z||000000||DreXteR||07-25-2001||03:36 AM||||Need info in wich parts of gm sb are interchangable with the 2.8~3.4 engines. I know that lifters are, but wich model?? <BR>If some1 can detail a list, I will appreciate it.<P>Thanx<P><BR>DreX<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://users.centennialpr.net/drexter/Fiero/Fiero1.jpg">  <BR>86 GT Turbo Intercooler Project - Total Restoration.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Leadfoot||07-25-2001||02:17 PM||||I think the 305 sb has interchangeable rocker arms. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||DreXteR||07-26-2001||02:25 PM||||Top.!||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||07-26-2001||03:27 PM||||No, the rockers won't fit without some work. About the only SB interchangeable parts are the cam bearings. It's a common upgrade.<P>TK||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||07-26-2001||03:27 PM||||Sorry, pouble dost.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 07-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||DreXteR||07-26-2001||03:38 PM||||Terryk - What about the lifters? A set of roller lifters would be great. <P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||07-26-2001||09:34 PM||||Not lifters, at least from everything I've seen and read. I believe Crane may still make the roller lifters and plates for the 660 engine. I know they still make the roller tip and true roller rockers (gold). I had the true's in my X-11. And they do clear the Fiero valve covers. I used them on the X-11 engine.<P>The Chevy Power book would have said if the SBC lifters would fit and it doesn't. It only says the rods (need to be narrowed .080") and cam bearings will work. Unless you are winding over 7k, the stock rods are fine.<P>The Chevy Power book is worth owning. Any GM dealer.<P><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 07-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||DreXteR||07-26-2001||09:52 PM||||Thanx for the info Terryk. I will try to reach the GM Powerbook. Ive never seen it, but maybe asking could get it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>BTW, this guy use roller rocker but dont specified. <A HREF="http://members.tripod.com/TurboZ24/Specs.htm" TARGET=_blank>Specs</A> and <A HREF="http://members.tripod.com/TurboZ24/" TARGET=_blank>Site</A><P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000008||terryk||07-26-2001||11:22 PM||||Crane makes roller rockers that fit. I had them in the X-11 engine. There were two versions. Now that I think about it, one version (mine) bolted right in. The others required the stud holes to be re-tapped. I wonder if those were the SBC rockers. I'm talking about true roller rockers, not roller tipped.<P>The Chevy Power book I have is PN 24502488 $19.95 from the dealer. I think this is the one that is still in print.<P>The details from the book are:<P>Aluminum Bow Tie Block 10051141<P>Use narrowed 67 or earlier connecting rods narrowed .086" o the large end and new bearing tang notches.<P>Pistons, 12.5:1 14044833 Std, 34 .5mm, 35 1.0mm. 14033129 stock 9.0:1, 31-32 are the oversized.<P>HO heads are 14054884. Don't muck with the vane....<P>It makes no mention of V8 lifters working. It does say that there are limitations to what lifters will work due to the difference in oiling. SealPower PN AT-992 mechanical lifters will work.<P>Yep, SBC roller rockers will work with new studs.Crane 11756. These might not clear the Fiero covers. The ones I had would. I can't find the part number.<P>HD oil pump is 10051104. Use with blue stripe spring (and some come with no stripe on them) 10044435 for 70 PSI.<P>So other usefiul details.<P>TK<BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 07-26-2001).]||||reg||1
